1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,360
Welcome to Finnie, a financial assistant with four focused agents.

2
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:10,465
Streamlit provides the interface, while LangGraph coordinates routing, validation, specialist execution, and report composition.

3
00:00:10,465 --> 00:00:14,825
Each analysis starts with validated inputs and deterministic Python calculations.

4
00:00:14,825 --> 00:00:21,801
Only then does it retrieve financial knowledge and ask a language model to explain the results.

5
00:00:21,801 --> 00:00:24,854
This keeps arithmetic separate from generated prose.

6
00:00:24,854 --> 00:00:28,342
The knowledge base is separate from user data.

7
00:00:28,342 --> 00:00:36,626
Chroma retrieves document chunks, optionally filters by category, ranks twenty candidates by vector distance, and selects the top five.

8
00:00:36,626 --> 00:00:40,115
These are similarity results, not proof of relevance.

9
00:00:40,115 --> 00:00:44,475
Chat has a separate context and only uses library knowledge.

10
00:00:44,475 --> 00:00:50,579
Session memory holds temporary reports; explicitly saved inputs belong to a local user profile.

11
00:00:50,579 --> 00:00:56,248
Identifying report fields are removed before model calls, while necessary financial values remain.

12
00:00:56,248 --> 00:00:58,864
All supported monetary inputs use U.S.

13
00:00:58,864 --> 00:00:59,300
dollars.

14
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,649
The chat agent specializes in financial education.

15
00:01:02,649 --> 00:01:06,055
A user can ask how diversification reduces concentration risk.

16
00:01:06,055 --> 00:01:11,353
Finnie retrieves library passages and generates a grounded explanation with document and page citations.

17
00:01:11,353 --> 00:01:14,759
Portfolio holdings and goal inputs never become chat context.

18
00:01:14,759 --> 00:01:19,300
When evidence is insufficient, the agent abstains instead of inventing an answer.

19
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,738
The portfolio agent reads supplied holdings from CSV or Excel.

20
00:01:23,738 --> 00:01:27,477
It calculates total value, asset allocation, sector exposure, and concentration.

21
00:01:27,477 --> 00:01:33,458
Here, Tech Heavy totals three hundred twenty thousand dollars, and the largest position is thirty percent.

22
00:01:33,458 --> 00:01:40,188
Effective holdings are about four point four, calculated as one divided by the sum of squared portfolio weights.

23
00:01:40,188 --> 00:01:44,300
Findings describe the holdings and supplied goal, without fetching replacement prices.

24
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,627
The market agent fetches historical end-of-day data through Alpha Vantage.

25
00:01:48,627 --> 00:01:53,342
It calculates period return, daily changes, annualized volatility, closing-price drawdown, and benchmark differences.

26
00:01:53,342 --> 00:01:59,870
Volatility is the sample standard deviation of daily returns multiplied by the square root of two hundred fifty-two.

27
00:01:59,870 --> 00:02:03,497
Drawdown measures the largest fall from an earlier closing peak.

28
00:02:03,497 --> 00:02:09,300
These describe the selected historical window; they do not predict future losses or explain market news.

29
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,256
The goals agent projects savings toward a target and deadline.

30
00:02:13,256 --> 00:02:19,441
It converts annual growth and fee assumptions to monthly rates, applies growth and fees, then adds the monthly contribution.

31
00:02:19,441 --> 00:02:21,720
Today's-dollar targets are adjusted for assumed inflation.

32
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:27,580
A cent-level binary search calculates the contribution needed to meet the target, with bounded deadline scenarios where allowed.

33
00:02:27,580 --> 00:02:36,370
In the house example, fifteen thousand dollars plus nine hundred monthly for thirty-six months reaches forty-seven thousand four hundred, leaving a twelve thousand six hundred dollar shortfall.

34
00:02:36,370 --> 00:02:39,300
Users can create multiple goals and analyze each separately.

35
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,723
Here is the persistence check.

36
00:02:41,723 --> 00:02:49,305
I saved the Tech Heavy holdings and the house-deposit goal to the Finnie Demo profile, then stopped and relaunched the Streamlit server.

37
00:02:49,305 --> 00:02:55,164
Selecting that profile still exposes both saved inputs, and they can be restored for a new analysis.

38
00:02:55,164 --> 00:02:59,300
Temporary conversations and reports are separate from these explicitly saved local inputs.

39
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,088
Finnie handles several failure paths.

40
00:03:02,088 --> 00:03:09,605
Invalid holdings or incomplete goals are rejected before calculations; the interface gives friendly guidance without exposing exception codes.

41
00:03:09,605 --> 00:03:15,451
Transient market API failures receive at most two retries with exponential backoff and jitter.

42
00:03:15,451 --> 00:03:22,133
If fetching still fails, eligible real cached data can be used with source and freshness information.

43
00:03:22,133 --> 00:03:31,738
Quote-level dummy defaults exist as a last resort, but the market risk engine does not use dummy history to calculate returns or volatility.

44
00:03:31,738 --> 00:03:36,749
If language generation or output validation fails, Finnie attempts one different model.

45
00:03:36,749 --> 00:03:42,178
When both attempts fail, analytical agents retain computed results and a local summary.

46
00:03:42,178 --> 00:03:46,354
Chat can abstain when a grounded answer cannot be prepared.

47
00:03:46,354 --> 00:03:47,607
Refusals are respected.

48
00:03:47,607 --> 00:03:52,201
Sanitized local logs record operational events without raw prompts or credentials.

49
00:03:52,201 --> 00:03:59,300
These recovery paths are covered by automated tests; the current suite has two hundred twenty-one passing tests.

50
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:03,840
The next improvements should strengthen evidence and financial depth.

51
00:04:03,840 --> 00:04:13,225
First, create a labeled retrieval evaluation set and measure precision at k and recall at k, alongside answer citation accuracy and latency.

52
00:04:13,225 --> 00:04:20,051
Second, extend portfolio analysis with expense ratios, fund look-through, and historical correlations when reliable inputs exist.

53
00:04:20,051 --> 00:04:26,024
Third, add probabilistic goal simulations, retirement withdrawals, pensions, and explicit shared-budget planning across goals.

54
00:04:26,024 --> 00:04:29,010
Those would extend today's deterministic accumulation model.

55
00:04:29,010 --> 00:04:36,689
Fourth, improve market coverage with adjusted total-return data and additional providers, while keeping source dates and freshness clear.

56
00:04:36,689 --> 00:04:40,955
A separate news synthesizer can later explain sourced market events.

57
00:04:40,955 --> 00:04:46,501
Finally, production use needs authentication, encrypted storage, stronger privacy review, and operational monitoring.

58
00:04:46,501 --> 00:04:52,901
Finnie currently provides an educational prototype: transparent calculations, retrieved financial context, and bounded model explanations.

59
00:04:52,901 --> 00:04:59,300
It does not execute trades or guarantee that an investment or savings target will succeed.
